course: dictionary
lesson: 4473
title: One word, many meanings: harness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A harness is a set of straps. You can wear one to keep you safe, or put one on an animal to control it. «A guide dog in a harness is working, so you do not stroke it.» The harness shows the dog is on duty, so you leave it alone.
explain: Harness can also be a verb, a doing word. To harness an animal means to put its harness on. To harness a natural force means to control it and use it. Scientists want to «harness the power of the wind» to make electricity.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. Near «safety» or «climbers», harness means a set of straps that holds a person. Near «power» or «electricity», it means to catch and use a force. Then swap in your meaning to check it fits.
fact: A harness is a set of straps.
fact: Harness can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A safety harness holds a climber, a window cleaner or a child safely.
fact: To harness a force means to control it and use it, such as the wind, sun or water.
fact: Stunts are only for trained professionals, never for copying at home.
exercise: «A guide dog in a harness is working, so you do not stroke it.» What does harness mean here? | A fast car on a road | A sweet meal eaten at one sitting | A tall tree in a park | * A set of straps put on an animal
exercise: Scientists want to «harness the power of the wind» to make electricity. What does harness mean? | To ignore completely | * To catch and use a natural force | To paint in bright colours | To sleep through the night
exercise: Which thing is a safety harness used for? | Watering plants | Drawing a map | * Holding a climber safely | Cooking a dinner
test: Window cleaners wear a «safety harness» high up on a building. What is a safety harness? | A set of paints | A bag for shopping | Straps that hold a person safely | * Straps that hold a person safely
test: «The farmer will harness the horse before the cart goes out.» What does harness mean here? | To sell the horse | To cook a meal | To wash the cart | * To put straps on an animal to control it
exam: Which word means to control a natural force and put it to use? | shillings | * harness | carrier | breakfast
